Problem: Which cities, stations, or sites spend the highest number of days/hours in Poor, Very Poor, or Severe AQI buckets?
----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Solution:
---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
I created Hours_Poor_to_Severe KPIs for cities and monitoring stations to count the recorded hours when the AQI was classified as Poor, Very Poor, or Severe.
I then used the Top_3_Poor_to_Severe measures to identify and display the three cities and stations with the highest number of these unhealthy hours.

DAX :  
----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Hours_Poor_to_Severe_City = 

 CALCULATE(
    COUNTROWS('goldlayer fact_cities'),
    'goldlayer fact_cities'[AQI Bucket] IN {"Poor","Very Poor","Severe"}
)

Top_3_Poor_to_Severe_cities = 
    VAR AQI_rank = IF(
        NOT ISBLANK([Hours_Poor_to_Severe_City]),
        CALCULATE(
            RANKX(ALLSELECTED('goldlayer fact_cities'[city]),
            [Hours_Poor_to_Severe_City],,DESC,Dense)
        )
    )
    
RETURN
IF(
    AQI_rank <= 3, [Hours_Poor_to_Severe_City],BLANK())


Hours_Poor_to_Severe_Station = 
CALCULATE(
    COUNTROWS('goldlayer fact_stations'),
    'goldlayer fact_cities'[AQI Bucket] IN {"Poor","Very Poor","Severe"}
)


Top_3_Stations_Poor_to_Severe_hour = 
VAR Aqi_station_rank = 
IF(
  NOT ISBLANK([Hours_Poor_to_Severe_Station]),
CALCULATE(
    RANKX(
        ALLSELECTED('goldlayer fact_stations'),
        [Hours_Poor_to_Severe_Station],,
        DESC,Dense
    )
),BLANK())

RETURN
IF(
Aqi_station_rank <=3, [Hours_Poor_to_Severe_Station],BLANK())
